# Design reference screenshots, regenerated by `npm run shots`. Binary and
# reproducible, so not carried in the repo; commit a specific before/after pair
# deliberately if a review needs one.
docs/design/shots/

# Provider secrets. server/.env.example carries the shape; these carry the
# values and must never be committed. The `.bak` glob matters: a timestamped
# backup of a secrets file is still a secrets file, and it is untracked rather
# than ignored unless it is named here.
server/.env
server/.env.local
server/.env.bak.*

# JetBrains IDE settings — local, not project configuration.
.idea/

# The server's DEFAULT data roots, which live inside the repo when
# PUBLISH_ROOT / IMAGE_ROOT are unset (`server/src/env.ts` defaults them to
# ./data/... so local development boots with no configuration).
#
# Ignored as belt-and-braces, not as the fix. The fix is setting those
# variables to host paths outside the repo — `server/.env.example` prescribes
# both — because anything in here is deleted by `git clean -fdx`, which takes
# every published page and every shared link with it. This entry only stops
# the second failure: a published page, which is author content, being
# COMMITTED. That already happened once (873bc6e, a stray Test Document that
# rode along in an unrelated bundle-ceiling commit and is still in this public
# repo's history).
data/
